<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">STUDENTS: Select a teacher or counselor who knows you and your abilities, and ask him/her to complete this form and return it to the Upward Bound Program, the school counseling office, or you. Please choose a teacher who has had you in an academic course (math, science, language arts, social studies). Choose a teacher who knows you well, even if you didn't earn the best grade in that class.</div>

  <div class="section-title">TEACHERS/COUNSELORS: We appreciate your assistance in completing this form. The student's application will not be complete until this recommendation form is received. Please return the form as soon as possible to the student, school counselor, or the Upward Bound Office (Fax: 970.491.1077).</div>

  <div class="section-title">What is Upward Bound?</div>
  <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">Upward Bound is a precollegiate program funded by the U.S. Department of Education and sponsored by Colorado State University. Upward Bound assists high school students with academic potential in developing the motivation and skills necessary to succeed in high school and enter college.</p>

  <div class="section-title">Who can participate?</div>
  <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">An individual is eligible to apply for Upward Bound if he/she:</p>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 10px;">
    <li>Is currently a freshman or sophomore in a target high school</li>
    <li>Is from a family whose taxable income does not exceed the limits set forth by federal regulations governing the program, or if neither parent has earned a four-year degree (Bachelor's degree).</li>
    <li>Is a U.S. Citizen or Permanent U.S. Resident</li>
    <li>Has academic potential but needs further development in academics, study skills or college exposure</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="section-title">How does Upward Bound work?</div>
  <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">During the school year, Upward Bound provides:</p>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 10px;">
    <li>Regular academic, personal, and college-prep advising for students at their high school, to help students set and reach their goals.</li>
    <li>Saturday sessions (UB University) help improve skills and performance in class and are 1-2 times a semester.</li>
    <li>Educational and cultural events and college visits to enrich student's experience and knowledge.</li>
    <li>A stipend for full effort and participation in Upward Bound.</li>
    <li>Assistance in securing admission and financial aid for college.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="section-title">During the Summer Program, Upward Bound Provides:</div>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 10px;">
    <li>A six-week intensive academic program.</li>
    <li>Individualized instruction through classes in math, literature, composition, laboratory science, foreign language, and college preparation.</li>
    <li>Recreational, cultural, and personal enrichment activities.</li>
    <li>High quality instructional and supervisory personnel.</li>
  </ul>

  <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 50px;">
    <img src="" alt="Logo" style="width: 150px; height: auto;">
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; margin: 0;">UPWARD BOUND</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin: 0;">COLORADO STATE UNIVERSITY</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">ACADEMIC INFORMATION</div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 15px;">
    <div>Date: <span data-field="academic_date">{{ academic_date }}</span></div>
    <div>Name: <span data-field="academic_full_name">{{ academic_full_name }}</span></div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 15px;">
    <div style="width: 30%;">First: <span data-field="academic_first_name">{{ academic_first_name }}</span></div>
    <div style="width: 20%; text-align: center;">Middle: <span data-field="academic_middle_name">{{ academic_middle_name }}</span></div>
    <div style="width: 30%;">Last: <span data-field="academic_last_name">{{ academic_last_name }}</span></div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    What kind of college/university are you interested in attending (check below)?
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 30px; margin-top: 10px;">
      <div><input type="checkbox"> Vocational/ technical college/ trade school/ technical institute</div>
      <div><input type="checkbox"> Two-year community college and/or transfer program</div>
      <div><input type="checkbox"> Four-year college/university</div>
      <div><input type="checkbox"> Undecided</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    What would you like to study in college? What type of career would like to have?
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    What are you currently doing to earn good grades?
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    What is keeping you from earning good grades?
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    What school and community activities (sports, clubs, volunteering, etc.) are you involved in this year?
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Please provide us with your most current grades OR end of semester grades.</div>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 10%;">PERIOD/SUBJECT</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">GRADE</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">DATE</th>
        <th style="width: 35%;">COMMENTS: effort, commitment, etc</th>
        <th style="width: 25%;">TEACHER'S INITIALS</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for i in range(1, 9) %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ i }}</td>
        <td><span data-field="grade_period_{{ i }}">{{ grade_period_{{ i }} }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="date_period_{{ i }}">{{ date_period_{{ i }} }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="comments_period_{{ i }}">{{ comments_period_{{ i }} }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="teacher_initials_{{ i }}">{{ teacher_initials_{{ i }} }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Information for Families and Students</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  h1, h2, h3 {
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .section-title {
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-top: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <h1>INFORMATION FOR FAMILIES AND STUDENTS</h1>
  <p>(Please keep this for future reference!)</p>

  <div class="section-title">What is Upward Bound?</div>
  <p>Upward Bound is a pre-college program funded by the U.S. Department of Education and sponsored by <span data-field="sponsor.name">{{ sponsor.name }}</span>. Upward Bound assists high school students with academic potential in developing the motivation and skills necessary to succeed in high school and enter college.</p>

  <div class="section-title">Who can participate?</div>
  <ul>
    <li>An individual is eligible to apply for Upward Bound if she/he:</li>
    <li>Is currently a freshman, sophomore or junior in a target high school</li>
    <li>Is from a family whose taxable income does not exceed the limits set forth by federal regulations governing the program, or if neither parent has earned a four-year degree (Bachelor's degree). (Strong preference is given to students who meet both conditions)</li>
    <li>Has academic potential but needs further development in academic or study skills</li>
    <li>Is a U.S. citizen or legal resident</li>
    <li>Is willing to make a long-term commitment of time and energy to improving himself/herself through the Upward Bound Program.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="section-title">How does Upward Bound work?</div>
  <p>During the school year, Upward Bound provides:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Regular academic, personal, and college-prep advising for students at their high school, to help students set and reach their goals.</li>
    <li>Saturday sessions (UB University) help improve skills and performance in class and are 1-4 times a semester</li>
    <li>Educational and cultural events and college visits to enrich student's experience and knowledge</li>
    <li>Assistance in securing admission and financial aid for college</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="section-title">During the Summer Program, Upward Bound Provides:</div>
  <ul>
    <li>A six-week intensive academic design to strengthen your academic skills for admission to college/university</li>
    <li>Individualized instruction through classes in math, literature, composition, laboratory science, foreign language, and college preparation</li>
    <li>Recreational, cultural, and personal enrichment activities</li>
    <li>High quality instructional and supervisory personnel</li>
  </ul>

  <p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">PLEASE SEE OTHER SIDE</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">What will be expected of the student?</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Enroll in eight academic courses every year (nine for trimester systems, four for block systems), including math, literature, composition, science, foreign language, and social studies. Students are expected to exceed the minimum high school course load recommended for admission to most colleges in the state:
      <ul>
        <li>4 years of math (including Algebra I, Geometry, & Algebra II)</li>
        <li>4 years of English (including speech, literature, composition)</li>
        <li>4 years of social studies (psychology, US history, geography, etc)</li>
        <li>2 years of the same foreign language, and</li>
        <li>3 years of laboratory science (biology, chemistry, physics, etc.)</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Achieve personal, academic, and college-prep goals, which are set by the student in consultation with the Upward Bound Advisor.</li>
    <li>Complete UB Scholar hours and attend the required sessions of UB University</li>
    <li>Participate in all program events and activities</li>
    <li>Maintain satisfactory academic progress and class attendance</li>
    <li>Attend each summer program</li>
    <li>Treat yourself, other students, and staff with respect, and be a positive representative of the program, your school, and your community.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="section-title">How can I help my daughter/son be successful in Upward Bound?</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Commit to transport son/daughter to high school where he/she will be picked up for events, trips, and the summer program.</li>
    <li>Participate in parent workshops on preparation for college, college admissions, financial resources to pay for college, career exploration</li>
    <li>Attend events during the academic year and summer program that highlight students' achievements and performance in the program.</li>
    <li>Agree to meet annually with an Upward Bound Advisor and maintain contact on an ongoing basis to assist your student in attaining personal, college-prep, and academic goals.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Upward Bound is free of charge. There is no financial obligation for families.</p>

  <p>Students who participate fully in the program develop the skills, confidence, and motivation necessary to succeed in high school, college and future careers. In recent years, 100% of Upward Bound participants have graduated high school, and over 90% have entered college following high school graduation.</p>

  <p>Upward Bound Contact Information:</p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="address.street">{{ address.street }}</span><br>
    <span data-field="address.city_state_zip">{{ address.city_state_zip }}</span><br>
    Phone: <span data-field="phone">{{ phone }}</span> Fax: <span data-field="fax">{{ fax }}</span><br>
    <span data-field="website">{{ website }}</span>
  </p>
</div>
</body>
</html>